{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (#5519) to add Base64 decode mode to `cmd/base64/main.go` by implementing SRD080-base64 requirements R2.1 through R2.4. Specifically:\n   - R2.1: Add `-d`/`--decode` flag to switch from encode to decode mode\n   - R2.2: Decode Base64 input back to binary data on stdout (whitespace ignored)\n   - R2.3: Add `-i`/`--ignore-garbage` flag to skip non-Base64-alphabet characters during decode\n   - R2.4: Report errors to stderr and exit non-zero when input contains invalid Base64 during decode (without `-i`)\n   \n   Design decision D1: Use `pkg/encutil.Decode` with a `DecoderConfig` whose `IgnoreGarbage` field is set from the `-i` flag.\n   \n   Only `cmd/base64/main.go` should be modified. No git commands should be run. The execution constitution requires: copyright headers, no functions over 40 lines, no scope creep, all files written before building/testing.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - `pkg/encutil.Decode(r io.Reader, w io.Writer, cfg DecoderConfig) error` - shared decode function\n   - `encutil.DecoderConfig{Decode func(string) ([]byte, error), IgnoreGarbage bool}` - decoder configuration\n   - `encutil.OpenInput(filename string) (io.ReadCloser, error)` - stdin/file input handler\n   - `encoding/base64.StdEncoding.DecodeString` - Go stdlib Base64 decoder to use as the Decode function\n   - `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - SIGPIPE handling required in all cmd/ utilities\n   - Manual arg parsing (no cobra) - the existing code uses hand-rolled flag parsing\n   - `syscall.EPIPE` error handling for graceful pipe closure\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd080-base64.yaml`\n     - Full SRD defining R1 (encoding, already implemented), R2 (decoding, to implement), R3 (exit codes/SIGPIPE)\n     - Non-goals: no Base64url, no Base32\n     - Key: R2.1 (-d/--decode), R2.2 (ignore whitespace), R2.3 (-i/--ignore-garbage), R2.4 (error on invalid without -i)\n\n   - `cmd/base64/main.go` (THE file to modify)\n     - Currently encoding-only, 145 lines\n     - `main()` calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`, `parseArgs()`, `encutil.OpenInput()`, `encutil.Encode()`\n     - `parseArgs(args []string) (int, string)` returns (wrap, file) - needs to also return decode and ignoreGarbage bools\n     - `encodeBase64(data []byte) string` wraps `base64.StdEncoding.EncodeToString`\n     - `parseLongFlag()` handles `--wrap`/`--wrap=` - needs `--decode` and `--ignore-garbage`\n     - `parseShortFlags()` handles `-w` - needs `-d` and `-i`\n     - `parseWrapFlag()` handles wrap value parsing\n     - Full current code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     package main\n     import (\n         \"encoding/base64\"\n         \"errors\"\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"strconv\"\n         \"strings\"\n         \"syscall\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/encutil\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         wrap, file := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n         rc, err := encutil.OpenInput(file)\n         if err != nil {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"base64: %s: %s\\n\", file, err.Error())\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         defer rc.Close()\n         err = encutil.Encode(rc, os.Stdout, encutil.EncoderConfig{\n             Encode:  encodeBase64,\n             WrapCol: wrap,\n         })\n         if err != nil {\n             if errors.Is(err, syscall.EPIPE) {\n                 os.Exit(0)\n             }\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"base64: %s\\n\", err.Error())\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n     }\n     func encodeBase64(data []byte) string {\n         return base64.StdEncoding.EncodeToString(data)\n     }\n     func parseArgs(args []string) (int, string) {\n         wrap := 76\n         var file string\n         i := 0\n         for i < len(args) {\n             arg := args[i]\n             if arg == \"--\" {\n                 if i+1 < len(args) {\n                     file = args[i+1]\n                 }\n                 break\n             }\n             if handled, advance := parseLongFlag(args[i:], &wrap); handled {\n                 i += advance\n                 continue\n             }\n             if arg == \"-\" || !strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"-\") {\n                 file = arg\n                 i++\n                 continue\n             }\n             i += parseShortFlags(args[i:], &wrap)\n         }\n         return wrap, file\n     }\n     func parseLongFlag(remaining []string, wrap *int) (bool, int) {\n         arg := remaining[0]\n         if !strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--\") {\n             return false, 0\n         }\n         if arg == \"--wrap\" || strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--wrap=\") {\n             return parseWrapFlag(remaining, wrap)\n         }\n         fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"base64: unrecognized option '%s'\\n\", arg)\n         os.Exit(1)\n         return false, 0\n     }\n     func parseWrapFlag(remaining []string, wrap *int) (bool, int) { /* ... handles --wrap and --wrap=N ... */ }\n     func parseShortFlags(remaining []string, wrap *int) int {\n         arg := remaining[0]\n         flags := arg[1:]\n         for j := 0; j < len(flags); j++ {\n             switch flags[j] {\n             case 'w':\n                 /* handles -w N and -wN */\n             default:\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"base64: invalid option -- '%c'\\n\", flags[j])\n                 os.Exit(1)\n             }\n         }\n         return 1\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `pkg/encutil/decode.go` (read-only, already implemented)\n    