riteria (AC1-AC4)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all four required files (srd080-base64.yaml, cmd/base64/main.go, pkg/encutil/decode.go, pkg/encutil/encode.go) and was about to begin implementing the changes to `cmd/base64/main.go`. No code has been written yet.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the modified `cmd/base64/main.go` with all changes in a single pass (per the implementation strategy in go_style_constitution), then run `go vet ./cmd/base64/` and `go test ./cmd/base64/... -count=1` to verify. The specific changes needed:\n   - Change `parseArgs` signature to return `(wrap int, decode bool, ignoreGarbage bool, file string)`\n   - Add `--decode` and `--ignore-garbage` to `parseLongFlag`\n   - Add `'d'` and `'i'` cases to `parseShortFlags`\n   - Add `decodeBase64(s string) ([]byte, error)` function wrapping `base64.StdEncoding.DecodeString`\n   - In `main()`, after opening input, branch on `decode` to call either `encutil.Encode` or `encutil.Decode` with appropriate config\n   - Pass additional `decode *bool` and `ignoreGarbage *bool` params through the parsing chain\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5519/b1e096d1-8edb-4a3f-8300-296399bbb76a.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b1e096d1-8edb-4a3f-8300-296399bbb76a","uuid":"1247829e-69c2-4b88-b908-7b884b37883e","timestamp":"2026-05-23T11:49:49.105Z","isSynthetic":true}
